    "pinning": "hookscript local:snippets/pin-102.sh: guest vCPU 0-11 -> host CPUs 0,2,...,22 (node 0, one physical core each); 12-23 -> 1,3,...,23 (node 1); hyperthread siblings 24-47 left to the host. Verified on the host with taskset after a full VM stop/start",
    "numa_binding": "numa0: cpus=0-11,hostnodes=0,policy=bind; numa1: cpus=12-23,hostnodes=1,policy=bind (32016 MB each). Verified on the host: /proc/<qemu pid>/numa_maps bind:0 region only on N0, bind:1 only on N1",
    "not_pinned": "QEMU main and I/O threads and host ZFS threads may run on the hyperthread siblings of the pinned cores",
    "pages": "4 KiB pages (no huge pages); TLB misses add to the latency figures for local and remote alike"
  },
